{"text": "MICHAEL D. WATERS GRANVILLE COUNTY COURTHOUSE\n101 MAIN STREET\n\nDISTRICT ATTORNEY\nNINTH PROSECUTORIAL DISTRICT OxForo, NC 27565\nP: (919) 690-4860, F: (919) 690-4861\n\nNovember 14, 2018\n\nHon. N. Lorrin Freeman\nWake County District Attorney\nP.O. Box 31\nRaleigh, NC 27602\n\nRE: Granville County Sheriff's Office\n\nDear Ms. Freeman:\n\n| understand that you have been contacted by the North Carolina State Bureau of Investigation\n(SBI), about a recording that | provided to them. | would like your assistance in assessing the recording,\nand determining whether the SBI should open an investigation into this matter.\n\nBy way of background information, | was provided this recording during my representation of\nJoshua Freeman, in August of 2014. At that time, | was still in private practice. After coming into\npossession of this recording, | contacted Special Agent John Spears at the Federal Bureau of\nInvestigation (FBI) in Cary. After speaking with him, | delivered a copy of this recording to him in August\nof 2014. | do not know if Special Agent Spears opened an investigation as a result of my meeting with\nhim or not.\n\nIn January of 2017, | met with Director Bob Schurmeier and Special Agent in Charge Mike\nDenning of the SBI. An Assistant Director was also in attendance, and he took possession of the\nrecording, but | understand that he left his position with the SBI shortly thereafter. On Tuesday,\nOctober 30, 2018, | provided another copy of the recording to Assistant Special Agent in Charge Lynn\nGay. | provided it after learning of an investigation in Granville County, and considered it relevant to\n\ntheir inquiry.\n\n| think, at this point, | would be considered a fact witness, and it would be appropriate for you to\nadvise the SBI about whether or not to open an investigation.\n\nSincerely,\n\nMMAS\n\nMichael D. Waters",
